{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "gr-sou",
  "connector": "〜そう",
  "gloss": "looks (like it will)",
  "title": "〜そう — looks tasty, looks like rain",
  "pattern": "い-adjective without い / な-adjective / ます form without ます + そう(だ)",
  "explanation": "そう after an adjective or a verb says how something looks: おいしそう — looks delicious; {高|たか}そう — looks expensive; {雨|あめ}が{降|ふ}りそう — looks like it’s going to rain. Drop the い of an い-adjective (おいし + そう), or the ます of a verb ({降|ふ}ります → {降|ふ}りそう). いい is irregular: よさそう.",
  "natural": "Reacting to what you see: わあ、{楽|たの}しそう！ — oh, that looks fun!",
  "stiff": "Watch out for かわいそう: it means “poor thing”, not “looks cute”. For what you plainly see, like a colour, just say it: {赤|あか}いね.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "gx-sou-1",
